Paces niri's refresh, the walk over every window that follows each wakeup
of its event loop, to at most once per frame of its fastest output. A
wakeup within a frame of the last refresh puts the walk off to one timer,
so every wakeup is still followed by a refresh within a frame, and a burst
of client commits by one. Input, an action, a keyboard focus change and a
window or layer surface coming or going refresh at once. Blockers, popups
and the keyboard's focus are still handled on every wakeup. niri's own
tests run unpaced, as written; those in src/tests/refresh_pacing.rs pace.
A trace line once a second says how many refreshes ran in how many
wakeups.

